                <pb facs="0761" n="661" sameAs="frus:frus1920v03/pg661"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">760i.61/19: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Commissioner at Riga</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Young</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Riga</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-09-13T16:00:00+01:36"><hi rendition="#italic">September 13,
                                1920—4 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received September 14—12:30
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>151. Your September 11th, 6 p.m. Instruction complied with. Though without any
                    evidence or proof, it is my opinion that inquiry regarding our naval vessels
                    emanates from Bolsheviks. Inquiry regarding consul apparently purely
                    Esthonian.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Young</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
